IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Taxation Administration Act 1953 (Commonwealth of Australia) -- what I must quote and what must be withheld from what I am
-- paid: tax file numbers (s 2 definition, s 8C(2), Part III Division 2 Subdivision BA, ss 8WA, 8WB); PAYG withholding as it
-- reaches the payee (Schedule 1 Part 2-5): which payments to me must have an amount withheld (ss 12-1, 12-10, 12-35, 12-190),
-- how much (ss 15-10, 15-15; Taxation Administration Regulations 2017 ss 5 "top rate", 26, 38), declarations to my payer
-- (s 15-50; Regulations s 56), when my payer withholds and pays it over (ss 16-5, 16-75, 16-95, 16-100, 16-105), what my payer
-- owes if it does not (s 16-30), my payer's discharge (s 16-20), my payment summary (s 16-155, read with s 389-20) and my credit
-- (s 18-15).
--
-- SEAT: the taxpayer -- here the individual who is paid: the employee being withheld from (Chloe, Daniel), and the sole trader
-- paid for supplies (Jake). "What must I quote, and what must be withheld from what I am paid?" Provisions addressed to the
-- payer are encoded as what they mean for the person paid: whether tax comes out of my pay, how much, when my payer must pay
-- it over, what I must be given.
--
-- Edition: Compilation No. 226, compilation date 27 August 2026 (includes amendments up to Act No. 79, 2026 and Act No. 82,
-- 2026), register id C2026C00393, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/C1953A00001.txt (four volumes in one file).
-- Regulations: Taxation Administration Regulations 2017, Compilation No. 17, compilation date 27 August 2026 (includes
-- amendments up to Act No. 82, 2026; register id F2026C00849), as deposited at
-- ../../../taxation-administration-regulations-2017/registers/source-bundle/F2017L01227.txt. The "top rate" of Regulations s 5
-- is brought in from the Income Tax Rates Act 1986 (Compilation No. 66, 1 July 2026, register id C2026C00300, Schedule 7
-- Part I, ../../../income-tax-rates-act-1986/registers/source-bundle/C2004A03348.txt) and the Medicare Levy Act 1986
-- (Compilation No. 53, 1 July 2026, register id C2026C00295, s 6(1),
-- ../../../medicare-levy-act-1986/registers/source-bundle/C2004A03351.txt).
--
-- NOT ENCODED. Income Tax Assessment Act 1936 Part VA (issuing TFNs, TFN declarations, s 202CB) -- that Act, not this one; the
-- scenarios' "Part VA of the Taxation Administration Act" does not exist. The withholding schedules made under s 15-25 (the
-- amount withheld from wages, including the no-TFN amount and the HELP component) -- NOT DEPOSITED, so the amount is an INPUT.
-- The higher amount than $50 that GST Act s 29-80(1) regulations may set -- an INPUT. Junior rates (Fair Work Act 2009) and
-- superannuation (Superannuation Guarantee (Administration) Act 1992). Subdivisions 12-C to 12-J, ss 12-40 to 12-60, Divisions
-- 13 and 14; the large withholder's weekday table (s 16-75(1)); the Commissioner's withholder-status determinations (ss 16-110,
-- 16-115) and the June 2001 and group limbs of ss 16-95, 16-100; the offence in s 16-25; part-year payment summaries (s 16-160);
-- s 8WC; refunds of over-withheld amounts (Subdivision 18-B).
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written with the writing-l4-rules skill from the individual's seat with the 2026-10-18 defaults. No
-- pipeline, no coverage table, no independent test pass, no human gate. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Taxation Administration Act 1953 -- tax file numbers and PAYG withholding`

§§ `s 2, s 8C(2) -- not quoting my TFN`

-- s 2(1): "tax file number means a tax file number as defined in section 202A of the Income Tax Assessment Act 1936."
-- s 8C(2): "a person shall not be taken to have refused or failed to furnish information to the Commissioner or another person
-- ... merely because the person has refused or failed to quote the person's tax file number". No provision of this Act obliges
-- an individual of any age to get or to quote a TFN.
@export Am I taken to have failed to give information, under s 8C, when I have not quoted my TFN?
GIVEN `I failed to give other information I was required to give` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you failed to give information other than your TFN that a taxation law required of you
      `I did not quote my TFN` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you refused or failed to quote your tax file number
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I taken to have failed to give information` IF
    `I failed to give other information I was required to give`

§§ `ss 8WA, 8WB -- who may ask for my TFN, and what they may do with it`

-- s 8WA(1): "A person must not require or request another person to quote the other person's tax file number." Penalty: "100
-- penalty units or imprisonment for 2 years, or both." (1AA): does not apply if "(a) provision is made by or under a taxation
-- law ... for the person to quote the number"; (b) the request is in connection with exercising powers or performing functions
-- under, or complying with an obligation imposed by, a taxation law (or a listed Commonwealth law); (c) the requester is "acting
-- on the other person's behalf in the conduct of the other person's affairs". (1A): a request so that the number can be put in an
-- application for an ABN. (2): asking for a document on which the TFN is recorded, if the other person may remove it first.
DECLARE `Request for my TFN` HAS
    `a taxation law provides for me to quote my TFN to them` IS A BOOLEAN
    `they ask in order to comply with or perform a function under a taxation law` IS A BOOLEAN
    `they act on my behalf in my affairs` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is for my ABN application` IS A BOOLEAN
    `they only ask for a document from which I may remove my TFN` IS A BOOLEAN

@export Does someone commit an offence under s 8WA by asking me for my TFN?
GIVEN `the request` IS A `Request for my TFN` @desc Who is asking for your tax file number, and why
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is it an offence to ask me for my TFN` IF
        (NOT `the request`'s `a taxation law provides for me to quote my TFN to them`)
    AND (NOT `the request`'s `they ask in order to comply with or perform a function under a taxation law`)
    AND (NOT `the request`'s `they act on my behalf in my affairs`)
    AND (NOT `the request`'s `it is for my ABN application`)
    AND (NOT `the request`'s `they only ask for a document from which I may remove my TFN`)

-- s 8WB(1): a person must not "(a) record another person's tax file number or maintain such a record; or (b) use [it] in a
-- manner connecting it with the other person's identity; or (c) divulge or communicate [it] to a third person." Penalty: 100
-- penalty units or 2 years, or both. (1A): not "(a) to the extent required or permitted by, or reasonably necessary in order to
-- comply with an obligation imposed by, a taxation law"; (b) in exercising powers or functions under such a law; (c) when acting
-- on the other person's behalf.
@export Does someone commit an offence under s 8WB by recording, using or passing on my TFN?
GIVEN `they record, use or pass on my TFN` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether they record your TFN, use it linked to your identity, or pass it on
      `a taxation law requires or permits it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a taxation law requires or permits it, or it is reasonably necessary to comply with one
      `they exercise a function under a taxation law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether they do it in exercising powers or functions under a taxation law
      `they act on my behalf` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether they act on your behalf in your affairs
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is it an offence to record, use or pass on my TFN` IF
        `they record, use or pass on my TFN`
    AND (NOT `a taxation law requires or permits it`)
    AND (NOT `they exercise a function under a taxation law`)
    AND (NOT `they act on my behalf`)

§§ `ss 12-1, 12-10, 12-35, 12-190, 16-5 -- must tax be withheld from what I am paid`

-- s 12-35: "An entity must withhold an amount from salary, wages, commission, bonuses or allowances it pays to an individual as
-- an employee". It asks neither the employee's age nor whether a TFN was quoted. s 12-1(1): need not withhold under s 12-35 "if
-- the whole of the payment is exempt income"; (1A): nor under Subdivision 12-B or s 12-190 if the whole payment is neither
-- assessable nor exempt income. s 12-10: the Division "does not apply to a payment in so far as it consists of providing a
-- non-cash benefit".
-- s 12-190(1): a payer must withhold from a payment for a supply made "in the course or furtherance of an enterprise carried on in
-- Australia by the other entity", unless: (2) the supplier's ABN is quoted on an invoice or other document; (4)(a) the payment is
-- not made in the course of the payer's own enterprise; (4)(b) the payment, net of GST, "does not exceed $50 or such higher amount
-- as is specified in regulations in force for the purposes of subsection 29-80(1) of the GST Act"; (6) an individual's written
-- statement that the supply is a hobby or wholly private, unless the payer has reasonable grounds to believe it false. ((3),
-- (4)(c), (d) and (5) are not modelled.) s 16-5: the payer "must do so when making the payment".
DECLARE `What I am paid for` IS ONE OF
    `salary or wages as an employee`
    `a commission, bonus or allowance as an employee`
    `a supply I make in my business`
    `a non-cash benefit`

DECLARE `My payment` HAS
    `what it is for` IS A `What I am paid for`
    `the whole payment is exempt income` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the whole payment is neither assessable nor exempt income` IS A BOOLEAN
    `my ABN is quoted on an invoice or other document` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the payer pays in the course of its own enterprise` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the payment net of GST` IS A NUMBER
    `the threshold set by GST regulations, or 50` IS A NUMBER
    `I gave a written hobby or private-supply statement` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the payer has grounds to think my statement false` IS A BOOLEAN

@export Must my payer withhold tax from this payment to me (ss 12-1, 12-10, 12-35, 12-190)?
GIVEN `the payment` IS A `My payment` @desc The payment made to you and what it is for
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must tax be withheld from my payment` IF
    CONSIDER `the payment`'s `what it is for`
    WHEN `a non-cash benefit` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a supply I make in my business` THEN
            (NOT `the payment`'s `the whole payment is neither assessable nor exempt income`)
        AND (NOT `the payment`'s `my ABN is quoted on an invoice or other document`)
        AND `the payment`'s `the payer pays in the course of its own enterprise`
        AND `the payment`'s `the payment net of GST` GREATER THAN `the payment`'s `the threshold set by GST regulations, or 50`
        AND ((NOT `the payment`'s `I gave a written hobby or private-supply statement`)
             OR `the payment`'s `the payer has grounds to think my statement false`)
    OTHERWISE
            (NOT `the payment`'s `the whole payment is exempt income`)
        AND (NOT `the payment`'s `the whole payment is neither assessable nor exempt income`)

§§ `ss 15-10, 15-15; Regulations ss 5, 26, 38 -- how much is withheld`

-- s 15-10(1): the amount Subdivision 12-B requires "is to be worked out under the withholding schedules made under section
-- 15-25. However, if the regulations prescribe how the amount is to be worked out, then it is to be worked out under the
-- regulations." s 15-15: the Commissioner may vary the amount, including to nil. s 15-30: the schedules must have regard to the
-- income tax and Medicare levy rates and the HELP repayment amounts, so the HECS component of a payslip is in the schedule. The
-- schedules are NOT DEPOSITED: the schedule amount is an INPUT.
@export How much must be withheld from my wages (ss 15-10, 15-15), given the withholding schedule amount?
GIVEN `the schedule amount` IS A NUMBER @desc The amount the withholding schedule gives for this payment, in dollars (an input: the schedules are not deposited)
      `the Commissioner varied it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commissioner has varied the amount for you under s 15-15
      `the varied amount` IS A NUMBER @desc The varied amount, in dollars (nil if varied to nil)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How much must be withheld from my wages` MEANS
    IF `the Commissioner varied it` THEN `the varied amount` ELSE `the schedule amount`

-- Regulations s 5: "top rate means the sum of: (a) the highest rate specified in the table in Part I of Schedule 7 to the Income
-- Tax Rates Act 1986; and (b) the rate of levy specified in subsection 6(1) of the Medicare Levy Act 1986." Rates Act Schedule 7
-- Part I, item 4 of each table: "exceeds $190,000 -- 45%". Medicare Levy Act s 6(1): "The rate of levy payable by a person upon a
-- taxable income is 2%." So 47%.
`the top rate in percent` MEANS 45 PLUS 2

-- Regulations s 26(2): "If the amount is less than $1, disregard the amount." (3): "If the amount is more than $1 and includes a
-- number of cents that is less than a whole dollar, disregard the number of cents".
GIVEN `amount` IS A NUMBER @desc An amount in dollars
GIVETH A NUMBER
`rounded down to whole dollars` MEANS
    IF `amount` LESS THAN 1 THEN 0 ELSE TRUNC `amount` 0

-- Regulations s 38(2): for a payment to which s 12-190(1) applies, "The amount to be withheld from the payment is an amount equal
-- to the product of the top rate and the amount of the payment." Both the payment and the product are rounded under s 26.
@export How much must my payer withhold from a payment for my supply when my ABN is not quoted (Regulations s 38)?
GIVEN `the payment` IS A NUMBER @desc The payment for your supply, in dollars
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How much is withheld when I quote no ABN` MEANS
    `rounded down to whole dollars` (`rounded down to whole dollars` `the payment` TIMES `the top rate in percent` DIVIDED BY 100)

§§ `s 15-50; Regulations s 56 -- declarations I give my payer`

-- s 15-50(1): an individual who expects a withholding payment and "wishes to have a matter relating to the individual's income tax
-- ... taken into account" may give the payer a declaration about it in the approved form. (3): an individual whose circumstances
-- change in relation to a matter stated in a TFN declaration may give a declaration about it.
-- Regulations s 56(1): "An individual to whom subsection (2) or (3) applies must give a new declaration in the approved form". (2):
-- the individual gave a declaration under s 15-50(1) or (3) about a matter and "the individual's circumstances change in relation
-- to the matter"; (3): the individual gave a TFN declaration "expressing a wish to reduce the amount withheld to correspond with
-- the tax-free threshold" and "becomes a foreign resident".
@export Must I give my payer a new declaration (Regulations s 56)?
GIVEN `I gave a declaration about a matter under s 15-50` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have given your payer a s 15-50(1) or (3) declaration about a matter
      `my circumstances changed on that matter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your circumstances have changed in relation to that matter
      `I claimed the tax-free threshold in my TFN declaration` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your TFN declaration asked for withholding to reflect the tax-free threshold
      `I have become a foreign resident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have since become a foreign resident
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I give a new declaration` IF
        (`I gave a declaration about a matter under s 15-50` AND `my circumstances changed on that matter`)
    OR  (`I claimed the tax-free threshold in my TFN declaration` AND `I have become a foreign resident`)

§§ `ss 16-20, 16-30 -- my payer's discharge, and what my payer owes if it does not withhold`

-- s 16-20(1): an entity that "(a) withholds an amount as required by Division 12 ... is discharged from all liability to pay or
-- account for that amount to any entity except the Commissioner."
@export Can my payer still be made to pay me the amount it withheld (s 16-20)?
GIVEN `my payer withheld it as Division 12 required` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the amount was withheld as Division 12 required
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can my payer still be made to pay me what it withheld` IF
    NOT `my payer withheld it as Division 12 required`

-- s 16-30(1): an entity (except an exempt Australian government agency) that "fails to withhold an amount as required by Division
-- 12 ... is liable to pay to the Commissioner a penalty equal to that amount." (ss 16-25, 16-35 to 16-43 not computed.)
@export What is my payer liable to pay the Commissioner if it does not withhold from my payment (s 16-30)?
GIVEN `the amount required` IS A NUMBER @desc The amount Division 12 required to be withheld, in dollars
      `it was withheld` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your payer withheld it
      `my payer is an exempt Australian government agency` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your payer is an exempt Australian government agency
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What does my payer owe for not withholding` MEANS
    IF `it was withheld` OR `my payer is an exempt Australian government agency` THEN 0 ELSE `the amount required`

§§ `ss 16-75, 16-95, 16-100, 16-105 -- when my payer must pay over what it withheld from me`

-- s 16-95(1)(b): a large withholder for a month if the amounts withheld "during a financial year ending at least 2 months before
-- the current month exceeded $1 million". s 16-100(1)(b): medium if not large and the amounts withheld "during a financial year
-- ending before the current month exceeded $25,000". s 16-105: small if "there is at least one amount withheld by the entity
-- during that month" and it is neither. "Exceeded": exactly $25,000 is not medium.
DECLARE `Withholder size` IS ONE OF
    `a large withholder`
    `a medium withholder`
    `a small withholder`
    `not a withholder this month`

@export What size of withholder is my payer for the month (ss 16-95, 16-100, 16-105)?
GIVEN `withheld in a year ended at least 2 months before` IS A NUMBER @desc Amounts your payer withheld in a financial year ending at least 2 months before this month
      `withheld in a year ended before this month` IS A NUMBER @desc Amounts your payer withheld in a financial year ending before this month
      `withheld this month` IS A NUMBER @desc Amounts your payer has withheld during this month
GIVETH A `Withholder size`
`What size of withholder is my payer` MEANS
    IF `withheld in a year ended at least 2 months before` GREATER THAN 1000000 THEN `a large withholder`
    ELSE IF `withheld in a year ended before this month` GREATER THAN 25000 THEN `a medium withholder`
         ELSE IF `withheld this month` GREATER THAN 0 THEN `a small withholder`
              ELSE `not a withholder this month`

GIVEN `month` IS A NUMBER @desc A calendar month, 1 to 12
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the last month of its quarter` MEANS
    IF `month` AT MOST 3 THEN 3
    ELSE IF `month` AT MOST 6 THEN 6
         ELSE IF `month` AT MOST 9 THEN 9
              ELSE 12

-- s 16-75(2): a medium withholder pays an amount withheld during a month "by the end of the 21st day of the next month". (2A): a
-- deferred BAS payer, "by the end of the 28th day of: (c) the next month unless the amount is withheld during December; or (d) the
-- next February if the amount is withheld during December." (3): a small withholder, "by the end of the 21st day of the month
-- after the end of that quarter". (4) table, deferred BAS payer: quarter ending 30 September -- 28 October; 31 December -- 28
-- February; 31 March -- 28 April; 30 June -- 28 July. A large withholder pays on the weekday table in (1): not modelled, NOTHING.
-- (Date rolls a month past 12 into the next year.)
@export By when must my payer pay the Commissioner the amount it withheld from me (s 16-75)?
GIVEN `the size` IS A `Withholder size` @desc Your payer's withholder size for the month
      `the day it was withheld` IS A DATE @desc The day the amount was withheld from you, ISO 8601
      `my payer is a deferred BAS payer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your payer is a deferred BAS payer
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`By when must my payer pay over what it withheld` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the size`
    WHEN `a medium withholder` THEN
        IF `my payer is a deferred BAS payer`
        THEN IF `m` EQUALS 12 THEN JUST (Date 28 (`m` PLUS 2) `y`) ELSE JUST (Date 28 (`m` PLUS 1) `y`)
        ELSE JUST (Date 21 (`m` PLUS 1) `y`)
    WHEN `a small withholder` THEN
        IF `my payer is a deferred BAS payer`
        THEN IF `q` EQUALS 12 THEN JUST (Date 28 (`q` PLUS 2) `y`) ELSE JUST (Date 28 (`q` PLUS 1) `y`)
        ELSE JUST (Date 21 (`q` PLUS 1) `y`)
    OTHERWISE NOTHING
    WHERE
        `m` MEANS DATE_MONTH `the day it was withheld`
        `y` MEANS DATE_YEAR `the day it was withheld`
        `q` MEANS `the last month of its quarter` `m`

§§ `ss 16-155, 389-20 -- my payment summary`

-- s 16-155(1): "Within 14 days after the end of a financial year, an entity (the payer) must give a payment summary (and a copy of
-- it) to another entity (the recipient) if: (a) during the year the payer made one or more withholding payments" (other than the
-- listed kinds, including s 12-190 payments) to the recipient. s 389-20(1): the payer "is not required to comply with a
-- requirement of ... (c) section 16-155 ... to the extent that it would relate to an amount that the entity has notified under
-- section 389-5 or 389-15" (single touch payroll). The financial year ends on 30 June, so the day is 14 July.
@export Must my employer give me an annual payment summary, and by when (ss 16-155, 389-20)?
GIVEN `I was paid withholding payments in the year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your payer made withholding payments to you in the financial year (not s 12-190 payments)
      `all of them were reported through single touch payroll` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your payer notified all of them to the Commissioner under s 389-5 or 389-15
      `the financial year ends in` IS A NUMBER @desc The calendar year in which the financial year ends (30 June)
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`By when must I be given a payment summary` MEANS
    IF `I was paid withholding payments in the year` AND (NOT `all of them were reported through single touch payroll`)
    THEN JUST (Date 14 7 `the financial year ends in`)
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `s 18-15 -- my credit for what was withheld`

-- s 18-15(1): "An entity is entitled to a credit equal to the total of the amounts withheld from withholding payments made to the
-- entity during an income year if an assessment has been made of the income tax payable, or an assessment has been made that no
-- income tax is payable".
@export What credit do I get for the tax withheld from me in the income year (s 18-15)?
GIVEN `total withheld in the income year` IS A NUMBER @desc The total withheld from withholding payments to you in the income year, in dollars
      `I have been assessed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an assessment (or a nil assessment) of your income tax for the year has been made
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What credit do I get for tax withheld` MEANS
    IF `I have been assessed` THEN `total withheld in the income year` ELSE 0
